485
00:46:59.691 --> 00:47:04.284
I mean, what do I get? My livelihood
got flushed away and went swirling.

486
00:47:06.517 --> 00:47:08.184
You ain't lost everything.

487
00:47:08.237 --> 00:47:13.116
Yeah, and maybe you're not
such a big shot either! Ow! Jesus!

488
00:47:14.077 --> 00:47:17.164
Fair enough. Catch.

489
00:47:18.164 --> 00:47:19.957
Aah! Jesus.

490
00:47:20.008 --> 00:47:22.368
Say hello to the last fellow
who wouldn't cooperate with me.

491
00:47:22.436 --> 00:47:24.503
What're you telling me?
You telling me this thing is real?

492
00:47:24.535 --> 00:47:28.054
All the power in the world
resides in the eyes, fella.

493
00:47:28.089 --> 00:47:32.021
Sometimes they're more useful
than the people who bear them.

494
00:47:32.101 --> 00:47:36.060
No, you're directly out of
your fucking mind! You know that!

495
00:47:37.721 --> 00:47:38.700
Yeah.

496
00:47:38.899 --> 00:47:43.573
Eyes see. It's one of the most important
things I learned from my sister.

497
00:47:43.645 --> 00:47:46.672
Sister? She's supposed to be
your sister?

498
00:47:46.726 --> 00:47:50.004
My father's daughter.
That's right.

499
00:47:50.258 --> 00:47:52.712
What's the matter,
you don't see the resemblance?

500
00:47:53.579 --> 00:47:55.538
Now, let's take it
from the top, friend.

501
00:47:56.106 --> 00:47:58.977
With a lot of detail.
What do you say?

502
00:47:59.339 --> 00:48:02.417
He had a bird with him.
Nearly pecked my face off.

503
00:48:02.579 --> 00:48:05.736
He told me to tell T-bird
that death was on its way.

504
00:48:05.775 --> 00:48:07.935
Whatever the fuck that means.

505
00:48:08.636 --> 00:48:11.656
Draven. He said his name
was Eric Draven.

506
00:48:12.695 --> 00:48:14.695
Want to relax that thing now?

507
00:48:14.735 --> 00:48:19.215
This bird man, he just happened
to let you live, huh?

508
00:48:19.294 --> 00:48:23.494
You sure you ain't making all of this up
just to save your own ass?

509
00:48:23.534 --> 00:48:26.134
I ain't making all this up.

510
00:48:26.161 --> 00:48:30.480
I ain't twisted
like you two fucks.

511
00:48:32.406 --> 00:48:33.926
All right.

512
00:48:38.631 --> 00:48:43.430
A boy and his bird.
Awful touching.

513
00:48:43.871 --> 00:48:44.984
Yeah.

514
00:48:53.410 --> 00:48:56.756
For fuck's sake, die, will ya?
Give me that thing.

515
00:49:03.022 --> 00:49:04.702
Thanks.

516
00:49:04.768 --> 00:49:06.968
Funboy said he saw
a black bird too.

517
00:49:07.762 --> 00:49:09.968
A big one.

518
00:49:10.009 --> 00:49:13.701
Then he choked to death
on his own blood.

519
00:49:13.753 --> 00:49:17.513
I'll have the janitor
come on up.

520
00:50:18.072 --> 00:50:19.958
You again.

521
00:50:19.979 --> 00:50:22.318
Are you lost or hungry?

522
00:50:22.358 --> 00:50:23.404
Hi.

523
00:50:27.317 --> 00:50:29.157
<i>♪ It can't rain all the time ♪</i>

524
00:50:29.237 --> 00:50:33.557
<i>♪ Can't rain all the time
Can't rain all the time ♪</i>

525
00:50:42.275 --> 00:50:44.875
I don't know how many times I
gotta tell you. We're in this together!

526
00:50:44.955 --> 00:50:47.755
One part falls, it all falls!

527
00:50:48.481 --> 00:50:51.154
- You know how long it took us to put this together?
- Yeah, a long time.

528
00:50:51.194 --> 00:50:53.674
That piece of ratshit made Tin Tin
into a fucking voodoo doll!

529
00:50:53.754 --> 00:50:55.754
Tin Tin was a dick.

530
00:50:55.834 --> 00:50:58.551
Tin Tin. Sheesh.

531
00:50:58.617 --> 00:51:02.793
Fire it up! Fire it up!
Fire it up! Fire it up!

532
00:51:02.873 --> 00:51:04.712
Fire it up!

533
00:51:08.385 --> 00:51:09.945
No Funboy.

534
00:51:09.998 --> 00:51:13.757
Probably still...
banging away on Darla.

535
00:51:17.951 --> 00:51:20.910
Smokes and road beers. Be quick.

536
00:51:22.277 --> 00:51:23.290
I'm on it.

537
00:51:53.012 --> 00:51:55.985
What the fuck are
you supposed to be, man?

538
00:51:58.185 --> 00:52:00.505
I'm your passenger.

539
00:52:07.337 --> 00:52:09.184
Drive.

540
00:52:13.816 --> 00:52:15.803
What's all this happy horseshit?

541
00:52:16.283 --> 00:52:18.396
Hey, T-bird! T-bird!

542
00:52:23.102 --> 00:52:26.221
- Oh, shit!
- What the fuck's the matter with you?

543
00:52:26.301 --> 00:52:30.141
Stupid asshair! You hit my car!

544
00:52:36.733 --> 00:52:41.220
What do you want, man?
Money? Drugs? I got it.

545
00:52:43.006 --> 00:52:45.240
We could use you.
You did Tin Tin.

546
00:52:45.285 --> 00:52:48.244
- This is business, right?
- Faster.

547
00:52:51.151 --> 00:52:53.104
You got that cream stuff?

548
00:52:55.397 --> 00:52:57.716
I hate this.
They can't even call it cream legally.

549
00:52:58.924 --> 00:53:00.310
What in the crap...

550
00:53:05.329 --> 00:53:08.049
Oh, look. Making us popular.

551
00:53:08.089 --> 00:53:10.688
When they flash us like that,
they ain't friends.

552
00:53:16.135 --> 00:53:19.395
This is Vehicle 48. We got us
a big, old, red hot rod.

553
00:53:21.767 --> 00:53:23.494
Turn.

554
00:53:24.887 --> 00:53:28.013
You got something personal, amigo,
we can work it out, right?

555
00:53:29.140 --> 00:53:30.400
Huh?

556
00:53:34.305 --> 00:53:35.632
Damn! Dead end!

557
00:53:40.551 --> 00:53:42.911
Look out!

558
00:53:46.251 --> 00:53:48.370
Oh, my God! Get outta the way!

559
00:54:00.109 --> 00:54:03.088
Holy shit! Goddamn foreign cars!

560
00:54:07.594 --> 00:54:09.008
Shit! Shit!

561
00:54:16.233 --> 00:54:19.607
Oh, I hate this.
This ain't good.

562
00:54:20.960 --> 00:54:23.953
T-bird! I got you, man! I'm comin'.

563
00:54:24.019 --> 00:54:26.298
Shit!

564
00:54:39.284 --> 00:54:41.483
Remember?
Yeah, I remember everything.

565
00:54:41.563 --> 00:54:44.910
But I don't know what...
What? Huh? What?

566
00:54:44.944 --> 00:54:47.604
What are you talking about?
No, no, no, no, no.

567
00:54:47.650 --> 00:54:50.564
You mean that place downtown?
Yeah, I remember her.

568
00:54:50.617 --> 00:54:52.801
We needed to put some fear
into that little lady.

569
00:54:52.821 --> 00:54:55.761
She wasn't going along
with our tenant relocation program.

570
00:54:55.841 --> 00:54:59.468
And her idiot boyfriend shows up
and turns a simple sweep-and-clear...

571
00:54:59.502 --> 00:55:02.640
into a total cluster fuck!
Who gives a shit?

572
00:55:02.720 --> 00:55:06.175
It's ancient history!
Why? What do you want?

573
00:55:06.235 --> 00:55:10.639
What is it? What?
Speak to me. Speak!

574
00:55:12.159 --> 00:55:13.959
Did you send us
these complaints?

575
00:55:15.458 --> 00:55:18.972
Come here!
"Abashed the devil stood."

576
00:55:19.039 --> 00:55:21.118
Does it get you sweaty?

577
00:55:21.872 --> 00:55:26.197
I know you. I know you.
I knew I knew you.

578
00:55:26.237 --> 00:55:30.157
I knew I knew you.
But you ain't you.

579
00:55:30.210 --> 00:55:33.969
You can't be you. We put you through
the window. There ain't no coming back.

580
00:55:34.517 --> 00:55:37.476
This is the really real world.
There ain't no coming back.

581
00:55:37.582 --> 00:55:39.862
We killed you dead.
There ain't no coming back.

582
00:55:42.843 --> 00:55:43.903
T-bird...

583
00:55:43.954 --> 00:55:46.982
There ain't no coming back!
There ain't no coming back!

584
00:55:49.867 --> 00:55:53.514
T-bird.

585
00:55:54.100 --> 00:55:56.833
"Abashed the devil stood...

586
00:55:57.047 --> 00:55:59.713
"and felt how awful goodness is."

587
00:56:00.133 --> 00:56:02.892
"And felt how awful goodness is."

588
00:56:16.564 --> 00:56:18.584
T-bird. T-bird.

589
00:57:06.410 --> 00:57:09.024
<i>This is the 7:00 a.m. edition
of Action News.</i>

590
00:57:09.104 --> 00:57:11.502
<i>For over a decade,
the night before Halloween...</i>

591
00:57:11.549 --> 00:57:15.583
<i>has had a darker and deadlier nickname
in the inner city, "Devil's Night"...</i>

592
00:57:15.663 --> 00:57:18.942
<i>the name given to what has become
an annual plague of arson.</i>

593
00:57:19.022 --> 00:57:24.182
<i>Last year over 200 blazes were reported,
and 11 people lost their lives.</i>

594
00:57:24.222 --> 00:57:29.181
<i>Firemen are preparing for what may become the
biggest and deadliest Devil's Night ever.</i>

595
00:57:29.261 --> 00:57:32.740
<i>The mayor has fire fighters
from all surrounding counties...</i>

596
00:57:32.820 --> 00:57:36.460
Do you like them up or over?
I can't remember.

597
00:57:38.700 --> 00:57:41.019
What are you doing?
I don't even like eggs.

598
00:57:41.099 --> 00:57:45.819
- Wait, you loved eggs.
- Yeah, when I was five.

599
00:57:46.320 --> 00:57:49.858
So what do you want now?
Black coffee and cigarettes?

600
00:57:50.143 --> 00:57:53.138
So what did you take
to become mother of the year?

601
00:57:53.936 --> 00:57:58.097
Oh, it wasn't drugs.
Someone kind of woke me up.

602
00:57:58.137 --> 00:58:03.696
- Who?
- Oh, it was nuts.

603
00:58:04.169 --> 00:58:08.776
You're acting weird. Did you win
the lottery or something, Darla?

604
00:58:11.375 --> 00:58:15.495
Oh, forget it. I never was
too good at this mommy shit.

605
00:58:16.202 --> 00:58:17.748
Over easy.

606
00:58:19.494 --> 00:58:24.014
I like 'em over easy... Mom.

607
00:58:34.305 --> 00:58:36.332
Hey, Albrecht.

608
00:58:39.332 --> 00:58:41.771
This is the third hit
in your 'hood in 24 hours.

609
00:58:42.012 --> 00:58:45.098
We just fished this out of the river.
He's fused to his own car.

610
00:58:45.145 --> 00:58:48.950
- We're gonna have to ID his teeth.
- His name is T-bird.

611
00:58:49.016 --> 00:58:50.269
Arson was his speciality.

612
00:58:50.316 --> 00:58:52.850
Looks like he zigged
when he should have zagged.

613
00:58:52.970 --> 00:58:56.816
- Case closed.
- Bull-fuckin'-shit.

614
00:58:57.303 --> 00:58:59.162
Come here.

615
00:59:02.928 --> 00:59:04.528
You're holding out on me.

616
00:59:05.261 --> 00:59:08.421
I got a goddamn vigilante killer
knocking off scumbags left and right...

617
00:59:08.474 --> 00:59:11.207
and you're covering up
for somebody.

618
00:59:11.287 --> 00:59:13.607
Who's the cartoon character
in the painted face?

619
00:59:14.060 --> 00:59:16.920
- Hey, you're the detective. Why don't you tell me?
- Okay.

620
00:59:16.960 --> 00:59:19.413
Gideon's blows all to hell and you're
having a chitchat with some weirdo...

621
00:59:19.446 --> 00:59:22.366
who winds up in T-bird's car
when it zigs instead of zags.

622
00:59:22.406 --> 00:59:24.838
Then you steal one of
my case files from homicide...

623
00:59:24.865 --> 00:59:27.058
and you're saying this is
just a fucking automobile accident?

624
00:59:27.105 --> 00:59:29.805
- Come on!
- Yeah. Good speech though.

625
00:59:29.838 --> 00:59:31.105
I didn't want to interrupt you.
It sounded good.

626
00:59:31.125 --> 00:59:33.444
You gotta write that shit down.

627
00:59:33.590 --> 00:59:35.364
All right, smart-ass.

628
00:59:35.877 --> 00:59:38.084
The captain's got a little
love note waiting for you.

629
00:59:38.137 --> 00:59:42.203
- Welcome to the first day of the rest of your suspension.
- Suspension?

630
00:59:42.610 --> 00:59:45.843
- For what?
- Misconduct.

631
00:59:48.017 --> 00:59:49.762
Yeah, give me the lab.

632
01:00:38.702 --> 01:00:40.908
<i>One for sorrow, two for joy...</i>

633
01:00:40.995 --> 01:00:44.200
- Come here.
<i>- three for a girl, four for a boy.</i>

634
01:00:48.660 --> 01:00:49.874
<i>Dancing...</i>

635
01:01:22.296 --> 01:01:23.909
Eric?

636
01:01:26.935 --> 01:01:29.089
Man, Sarah, you're going crazy.

637
01:01:30.882 --> 01:01:32.469
Gabriel.

638
01:01:33.874 --> 01:01:35.401
I thought you were dead.

639
01:01:36.421 --> 01:01:38.687
You're not dead, are you?

640
01:02:03.390 --> 01:02:05.017
I knew it was you.

641
01:02:08.004 --> 01:02:09.584
Even with the make-up.

642
01:02:15.523 --> 01:02:17.742
I remembered your song.

643
01:02:17.822 --> 01:02:20.916
You said,
"Can't rain all the time."

644
01:02:21.502 --> 01:02:23.236
That is from your song, right?

645
01:02:34.660 --> 01:02:37.140
Come on, Eric. I know you're here.

646
01:02:39.733 --> 01:02:42.746
I miss you... and Shelly.

647
01:02:46.724 --> 01:02:49.618
Get so lonely all by myself.

648
01:02:52.244 --> 01:02:55.817
The hell with you.
I thought you cared.

649
01:02:56.658 --> 01:02:58.897
Sarah, I do care.

650
01:03:09.995 --> 01:03:11.695
That's him. That him!

651
01:03:11.741 --> 01:03:14.981
But he looked different. He was all painted
up white like some kind of dead whore.

652
01:03:15.055 --> 01:03:18.174
I seen him. T-bird, he sent me in
for some road beers, right?

653
01:03:18.268 --> 01:03:20.508
Then he took him away.
But I chased him down.

654
01:03:20.541 --> 01:03:23.453
And he flash fried T-bird
to his fucking car!

655
01:03:23.533 --> 01:03:26.893
Aw, T-bird!
Here's to you, buddy.

656
01:03:26.973 --> 01:03:30.732
Maybe we oughta just videotape this.
Play it back in slow motion.

657
01:03:32.005 --> 01:03:36.978
- Fire it up! Fire it up! Fire it up! Fire it up!
- You see the grave?

658
01:03:37.032 --> 01:03:38.971
- Empty.
- Fire it...

659
01:03:39.051 --> 01:03:41.531
Grave? What grave?

660
01:03:41.584 --> 01:03:43.091
What about my fucking grave?

661
01:03:43.577 --> 01:03:44.837
Three out of four.

662
01:03:44.884 --> 01:03:47.650
He's working his way back
to this speed freak right here.

663
01:03:47.730 --> 01:03:50.250
It's not fair.
It's Funboy's fault.

664
01:03:50.330 --> 01:03:53.369
That boy was out of control.
T-bird, he came in, he says...

665
01:03:53.555 --> 01:03:57.364
"Waste them both." And now
this ghost gonna kill my ass next!

666
01:04:00.808 --> 01:04:03.454
This ghost gonna
kill my ass next.

667
01:04:04.434 --> 01:04:07.128
- This ghost gonna kill...
- Hey.

668
01:04:07.307 --> 01:04:09.186
That ain't no ghost.

669
01:04:10.927 --> 01:04:13.967
- They have all arrived.
- Watch him.

670
01:04:14.460 --> 01:04:16.379
We might need him.

671
01:04:17.366 --> 01:04:19.726
Ghost gonna kill my...

672
01:04:32.117 --> 01:04:34.637
He like his plain
or with onions?

673
01:04:36.297 --> 01:04:38.484
Fine. Don't talk to me.

674
01:04:39.384 --> 01:04:43.090
When someone's dead,
they can't come back, can they?

675
01:04:43.700 --> 01:04:45.642
That's what I thought.

676
01:04:46.007 --> 01:04:48.247
Are you referring
to anyone in particular?

677
01:04:48.287 --> 01:04:50.602
You'll just think I'm nuts.

678
01:04:50.787 --> 01:04:54.121
Yeah, well, then maybe
they'll have to lock us both up.

679
01:04:54.444 --> 01:04:59.321
- You seen him too?
- I saw somebody.

680
01:04:59.991 --> 01:05:02.760
Maybe it was
your fairy godfather.

681
01:05:03.577 --> 01:05:05.835
Eric didn't come back for me.

682
01:05:05.901 --> 01:05:09.441
He can't be my friend anymore
because I'm alive.

683
01:05:11.115 --> 01:05:13.406
You want a friend
to walk you home?

684
01:05:42.388 --> 01:05:46.101
♪ I am the wicked
I am the wave of the future ♪

685
01:05:58.533 --> 01:05:59.806
♪ Being crucified ♪

686
01:05:59.853 --> 01:06:04.372
♪ You things, things, things of the flesh ♪

687
01:06:04.432 --> 01:06:06.672
♪ Do it slow ♪

688
01:06:06.712 --> 01:06:10.865
♪ Down avenues "cut me" ♪

689
01:06:10.912 --> 01:06:14.431
♪ Lust my eyes ♪

690
01:06:14.451 --> 01:06:21.023
♪ Licking lips encouraging Mr. Careworn ♪

691
01:06:21.076 --> 01:06:26.443
♪ To gaze upon the screen bask on ♪

692
01:06:26.476 --> 01:06:29.276
♪ After the flesh ♪

693
01:06:43.667 --> 01:06:44.733
Boys.

694
01:06:46.947 --> 01:06:49.993
It seems our friend T-bird won't be
joining us this evening...

695
01:06:50.053 --> 01:06:51.906
on account of
a slight case of death.

696
01:06:52.826 --> 01:06:53.865
You wanna sit down?

697
01:06:57.832 --> 01:06:59.326
Well, well, well.

698
01:06:59.379 --> 01:07:02.104
Devil's Night is upon us again.

699
01:07:02.144 --> 01:07:04.024
I thought we'd throw
a little party...

700
01:07:04.064 --> 01:07:07.223
start a bunch of fires,
make a little profit.

701
01:07:07.263 --> 01:07:09.423
I like the pretty lights.

702
01:07:11.649 --> 01:07:15.829
Problem is, it's all been done before.
You see what I'm saying?

703
01:07:15.883 --> 01:07:21.562
- That's no reason to quit.
- Wrong. Best reason to quit.

704
01:07:21.662 --> 01:07:23.461
Only reason to quit.

705
01:07:24.602 --> 01:07:27.842
A man has an idea.

706
01:07:29.055 --> 01:07:31.435
The idea attracts others...

707
01:07:31.469 --> 01:07:33.140
like-minded.

708
01:07:33.613 --> 01:07:35.220
The idea expands.

709
01:07:35.300 --> 01:07:38.779
The idea becomes an institution.

710
01:07:39.906 --> 01:07:41.906
What was the idea?

711
01:07:42.813 --> 01:07:45.098
See, that's what's
been bothering me, boys.

712
01:07:45.299 --> 01:07:47.693
But I'll tell ya, when I used
to think about the idea itself...

713
01:07:47.739 --> 01:07:50.386
it'd put a big old smile on my face.

714
01:07:51.679 --> 01:07:53.057
You see, gentlemen...

715
01:07:53.743 --> 01:07:57.937
greed is for amateurs.

716
01:07:58.270 --> 01:08:02.976
Disorder, chaos, anarchy...

717
01:08:03.196 --> 01:08:04.869
now that's fun!

718
01:08:04.902 --> 01:08:07.815
- What about Devil's Night?
- What about it?

719
01:08:08.022 --> 01:08:11.055
I started the first fires
in this goddamn city.

720
01:08:11.088 --> 01:08:14.175
Before I knew it, every charlatan
and shitheel was imitating me.

721
01:08:14.655 --> 01:08:17.574
Do you know what they got now?

722
01:08:18.035 --> 01:08:20.628
Devil's Night greeting cards.

723
01:08:22.061 --> 01:08:23.668
Isn't that precious?

724
01:08:24.653 --> 01:08:25.701
Yeah.

725
01:08:26.848 --> 01:08:31.332
The idea has become
the institution, boys.

726
01:08:31.953 --> 01:08:33.332
Time to move along.

727
01:08:33.412 --> 01:08:35.932
You don't want us to do
"Light My Fire" time for the whole city?

728
01:08:36.173 --> 01:08:38.211
No.

729
01:08:38.251 --> 01:08:40.771
No, I want you to set
a fire so goddamn big...

730
01:08:40.811 --> 01:08:43.811
the gods will notice us again.
That's what I'm saying.

731
01:08:44.077 --> 01:08:46.244
I want all of you boys to be able
to look me straight in the eye...

732
01:08:46.296 --> 01:08:50.696
one more time and say,
"Are we having fun or what?"

733
01:08:50.809 --> 01:08:52.769
- Hey, you! What's your name?
- Huh?

734
01:08:52.809 --> 01:08:54.689
Skank! You don't feel that?

735
01:08:54.729 --> 01:08:57.116
I feel like a little worm
on a big fucking hook.

736
01:08:57.683 --> 01:09:00.288
"I feel like a little worm
on a big fucking hook."

737
01:09:00.368 --> 01:09:04.568
Well, boy, your mama
must be damn proud of you!

738
01:09:07.388 --> 01:09:09.447
How the hell did
that thing get in here?

739
01:09:10.926 --> 01:09:12.073
Gentlemen.

740
01:09:14.727 --> 01:09:18.126
Let me go!
Let me go! I gotta go!

741
01:09:22.491 --> 01:09:25.725
You're him, huh? The avenger.

742
01:09:26.131 --> 01:09:28.165
The killer of killers.

743
01:09:28.798 --> 01:09:30.964
Nice outfit.

744
01:09:31.004 --> 01:09:33.004
I'm not sure
about the face though.

745
01:09:33.843 --> 01:09:35.697
I just want him.

746
01:09:36.157 --> 01:09:38.403
Well, you can't have him.

747
01:09:38.810 --> 01:09:41.043
Well...

748
01:09:43.369 --> 01:09:45.728
I see you have
made your decision.

749
01:09:46.922 --> 01:09:48.571
Now let's see you enforce it.

750
01:09:48.617 --> 01:09:51.890
Aw, this is already boring the shit
out of me. Kill him!

751
01:09:57.901 --> 01:10:00.594
Ooh, that had to hurt.

752
01:10:03.321 --> 01:10:04.560
Well, that's that.

753
01:10:05.540 --> 01:10:07.812
That guy was crazy.

754
01:10:14.038 --> 01:10:15.758
He's gone.

755
01:10:23.637 --> 01:10:25.277
Get him!

756
01:10:41.515 --> 01:10:44.701
Right here! Here, help me!
Help me! He's gonna kill me!

757
01:10:48.994 --> 01:10:50.474
Jesus Christ!

758
01:11:06.344 --> 01:11:07.784
Hey!

759
01:11:39.647 --> 01:11:41.227
You're all going to die.

760
01:11:55.392 --> 01:11:57.405
Get the fuck outta here!

761
01:12:32.660 --> 01:12:35.460
Guess it's not a good day
to be a bad guy, huh, Skank?

762
01:12:35.540 --> 01:12:38.619
I'm not Skank.
There's Skank right there.

763
01:12:39.620 --> 01:12:42.419
- Skank's dead.
- That's right.

764
01:12:42.745 --> 01:12:44.464
No!

765
01:12:51.024 --> 01:12:52.511
What in the crap...

766
01:12:53.524 --> 01:12:55.977
- Don't move!
- Hold it!

767
01:12:56.358 --> 01:12:59.336
That's all she wrote!
Move and we shoot!

768
01:13:07.514 --> 01:13:11.255
<i>You are surrounded by police units.
Do not attempt to escape.</i>

769
01:13:14.474 --> 01:13:17.287
<i>- Stop running immediately.</i>
- Holy shit!

770
01:13:17.320 --> 01:13:19.360
<i>Arms and legs...</i>

771
01:13:24.913 --> 01:13:29.512
<i>Stop immediately.
Lie down, spread your arms and legs...</i>

772
